// =============================================================================
// Academic Word List — IELTS / academic English, with Uzbek translations.
//
// Headwords follow Coxhead's Academic Word List (2000), which groups ~570 word
// families into ten sublists ordered by how often they appear in academic text:
// sublist 1 is the most frequent, sublist 10 the least. A learner working
// through them in order meets the highest-value words first.
//
// Deliberately no IPA and no example sentences here. The curated bank in
// `bilingual.ts` carries those because each entry there was checked by hand; at
// this scale a guessed transcription would teach a wrong pronunciation silently,
// and no transcription is better than a wrong one. Translations are the part
// that matters most for an Uzbek learner, so that is what this file commits to.
// =============================================================================

